  SEXES <- c( "Female",
 "Male")
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
  adSAMPYEARS <- 1995:2000    # when our "adults" were sampled
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
  adAGES <- 6:9               # ...
 of adults (ie potential parents)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
  juSAMPYEARS <- 1990:1999    # when our potential offspring were sampled
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
  juAGES <- 1:3               # ...
 and their range of ages at sampling
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
  juBYEARS <- (1990-3):(1999-1)  # implied range of juvenile birth-years
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
  # Any old values for fecundity-at-age...
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
  fec_SA <- autoloop( S=SEXES,
 A=adAGES,
 log( A))
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
  
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
  # Any old values for total fecundity over the years...
 say from 1e6 typical age-7 adults
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
  totfec_SB <- autoloop( S=SEXES,
 B=juBYEARS,
 1e6 * fec_SA[ S,
 7])
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
  try( Pr_POP_SYAYA <- autoloop( 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
      Sa=SEXES,
 Ya=adSAMPYEARS,
 Aa=adAGES,
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
      Yj=juSAMPYEARS,
 Aj=juAGES,
 {  # curly required coz multiple statements
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    Bj <- Yj - Aj;
                  # birth of Our juvenile
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    Aa_at_Bj <- Aa - (Ya - Bj);
     # how old was Our adult then?
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    Pr <- ifelse( Ya >= Bj,
         # was adult still alive then?
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
      fec_SA[ Sa,
 Aa_at_Bj] / totfec_SB[ Sa,
 Bj],
  # yes:
 competing against other adults
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
      0)                            # no:
 dead already
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    return( Pr)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
   }))
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
@
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Well,
 that didn't work,
 but at least the error message gives you a chance to figure out why.
 The problem is with accessing 
\family typewriter
fec_SA[Sa,Aa_at_Bj]
\family default
 and clearly 
\family typewriter
Sa
\family default
 won't be the cause,
 so it must be 
\family typewriter
Aa_at_Bj
\family default
 .
 The error message doesn't show you 
\family typewriter
Aa_at_Bj
\family default
 directly
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
While producing this example,
 I have started to think that the error message should include 
\emph on
all
\emph default
 available variables (including ones just calculated),
 not just the indices,
 because that might clarify things a lot!
 Next version...
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 because it's calculated only within the expression,
 but we can see where it came from.
 With 
\family typewriter
Ya=1995,Aa=9,Yj=1992,Aj=1
\family default
 we would have 
\family typewriter
Bj=1992-1=1991
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
Ya-Bj=1995-1991=4
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
Aa_at_Bj=9-4=5
\family default
.
 But the range of adult ages,
 
\family typewriter
adAGES
\family default
,
 which indexes 
\family typewriter
fec_SA
\family default
,
 is only 6:9.
 So the real problem is that our "adult" wasn't adult back then;
 s/he was too young.
 (The calculation could even have led to a negative age for the adult,
 if the juvenile was born before s/he was!) While we're at it,
 there is also the possibility of exceeding the maximum adult age—
 it won't be the case in the samples,
 because sampling kills the adults,
 but if we compare an adult to a juvenile born 
\emph on
after
\emph default
 the adult capture,
 then er 
\emph on
projected
\emph default
 age could be OOB.
 Let's fix that quickly:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
<<ifelse-still-naive>>=
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
  try( Pr_POP_SYAYA <- autoloop( 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
      Sa=SEXES,
 Ya=adSAMPYEARS,
 Aa=adAGES,
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
      Yj=juSAMPYEARS,
 Aj=juAGES,
 {
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    Bj <- Yj - Aj;
                  # birth of Our juvenile
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    Aa_at_Bj <- Aa - (Ya - Bj);
     # how old was Our adult then?
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
    Pr <- ifelse( 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
        (Ya >= Bj) &                   # too dead;
 note single ampersand coz vector
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
        (Aa_at_Bj >= min( adAGES)) &   # too young
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
        (Aa_at_Bj <= max( adAGES)),
    # too old in future (and will actually be already dead!)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
      fec_SA[ Sa,
 Aa_at_Bj] / totfec_SB[ Sa,
 Bj],
  # yes:
